                <pb facs="0296" n="274" xml:id="pg274"/>

                <head>118. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On August 11, 1961, McGeorge Bundy transmitted a memorandum to Secretary Rusk
                    which constituted National Security Action Memorandum No. 65 setting forth the
                    President’s decisions following review of the Joint Action Program submitted on
                    July 14 (see <ref target="#d93">Document 93</ref>). For text of NSAM No. 65, see
                        <hi rendition="#italic">United States-Vietnam Relations, 1945-1967</hi>,
                    Book 11, pages 241-244.</p>
            </div>
